        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "1ba3bb74",
          "name": "Evaluate Forward Declaration",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Evaluate Forward Declaration\n\n!_method\n\n\nEvaluate a simple arithmetic expression, e.g. \"2(1+3)/4\" or \"7 * 3\".\nSupports + - * / % ^, parentheses, unary plus/minus, implicit\nmultiplication (\"2(1+3)\") and decimal numbers.\n\nOn success returns true and the formatted result in `result`; on\nfailure returns false and an explanation in `result`.",
          "children": [
          ]
        }
        ]
      }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "213f3ac2",
      "name": "clipboard",
      "expanded": false,
      "text": "",
      "children": [
      {
        "id": "837d12ab",
        "name": "clipboard.hpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "8d0c63e8",
          "name": "Reading the Clipboard",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Reading the Clipboard",
          "children": [
          {
            "id": "3c7ba4f2",
            "name": "Linux - Use Xclip",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Linux - Use Xclip\n\nconst char* commands[] = {\n    \"wl-paste --no-newline 2>/dev/null\",\n    \"xclip -o -selection clipboard 2>/dev/null\",\n    \"xsel -o --clipboard 2>/dev/null\",\n};",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "2da147ae",
            "name": "Windows - Use OpenClipboard",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Windows - Use OpenClipboard\n\nif (!OpenClipboard(nullptr)) return \"\";",
            "children": [
            ]
          }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6c6fdf00",
          "name": "Storing in the Clipboard",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Storing in the Clipboard",
          "children": [
          {
            "id": "1b756736",
            "name": "Linux - Use Xclip",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Linux - Use Xclip\n\nconst char* commands[] = {\n    \"wl-copy 2>/dev/null\",\n    \"xclip -i -selection clipboard 2>/dev/null\",\n    \"xsel --input --clipboard 2>/dev/null\",\n};\nfor (const char* cmd : commands)\n{\n    FILE* pipe = popen(cmd, \"w\");\n    if (pipe == nullptr) continue;\n    std::fwrite(text.data(), 1, text.size(), pipe);\n    const int rc = pclose(pipe);\n    if (rc == 0) return true;\n}",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "bb2cf5ce",
            "name": "Windows - Use OpenClipboard",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Windows - Use OpenClipboard\n\nconst int wlen = MultiByteToWideChar(CP_UTF8, 0, text.c_str(), -1, nullptr, 0);\nif (wlen <= 1) return false;\nstd::wstring wide(static_cast<std::size_t>(wlen), 0);\nMultiByteToWideChar(CP_UTF8, 0, text.c_str(), -1, &wide[0], wlen);\n\nif (!OpenClipboard(nullptr)) return false;\nif (!EmptyClipboard())\n{\n    CloseClipboard();\n    return false;\n}",
            "children": [
            ]
          }
          ]
        }
        ]
      }
      ]
    },
