          "text": "Is Editor in Visual Mode\n\nSignature: bool IsVisualMode(Mode m)\nMethod: IsVisualMode\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    m Mode",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "96cd3a8f",
          "name": "Parse Replacement Arguments",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Parse Replacement Arguments\n\nSignature: bool ParseReplaceArgs(const std::string& args, std::string& old_text, std::string& new_text)\nMethod: ParseReplaceArgs\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    args     const std::string&\n    old_text std::string&\n    new_text std::string&\n\nSplit \"old/new\" at the first unescaped '/'. A backslash-slash\n(\"\\/\") is a literal slash and is unescaped in both parts. Returns\nfalse when no separator is present.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "8c5d1e9a",
          "name": "Read Clipboard",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Read Clipboard\n\nSignature: std::string ReadClipboard()\nMethod: ReadClipboard\nReturns: std::string\n\nRead the system clipboard (Win32 API on Windows, wl-paste/xclip/xsel\non POSIX). Returns \"\" when nothing is available or the clipboard is\nempty.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "323ca9bf",
          "name": "Scroll Past Helper",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Scroll Past Helper\n\n!_method\n\n\nA transparent leaf node that records the height of the box it is\nassigned each frame. Rendered as an overlay share of the editor view,\nit reports the editor's viewport height so the trailing scroll-past-\nbottom padding can be sized to about half the viewport (Vim-like).",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "65d7a389",
          "name": "Split Line Into Cells",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Split Line Into Cells\n\nSignature: std::vector<std::string> SplitCells(const std::string& line)\nMethod: SplitCells\nReturns: std::vector<std::string>\nParameters:\n    line const std::string&\n\nThis is used when creating / updating tables.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "bb6b7abd",
          "name": "Table Divider Line Check",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Table Divider Line Check\n\nSignature: bool IsDividerLine(const std::string& s)\nMethod: IsDividerLine\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    s const std::string&\n\nA markdown table separator row: \"| --- | --- |\", \"+-----+-----+\" or\na bare \"----\" (the web app's dividerPattern).",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "073e6359",
