            "id": "1ac8444a",
            "name": "Public Members",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Public Members",
            "children": [
            {
              "id": "e0380d55",
              "name": "Constructor",
              "expanded": false,
              "text": "Constructor\n\nSignature: Editor(std::shared_ptr<EditorState> state) : state_(std::move(state))\nConstructor: Editor\nParameters:\n    state std::shared_ptr<EditorState>\nInitializers:\n    state_ std::move(state)",
              "children": [
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "b5b7722d",
              "name": "Focusable Const",
              "expanded": false,
              "text": "Focusable Const\n\nbool Focusable() const override\n{\n    return true;\n}",
              "children": [
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "adcb0629",
              "name": "Ftxui Event",
              "expanded": false,
              "text": "Ftxui Event\n\nSignature: bool OnEvent(ftxui::Event event) override\nMethod: OnEvent\nReturns: bool\nQualifiers: override\nParameters:\n    event ftxui::Event",
              "children": [
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "371eef95",
              "name": "Render the Editor",
              "expanded": false,
              "text": "Render the Editor\n\nSignature: ftxui::Element Render() override\nMethod: Render\nReturns: ftxui::Element\nQualifiers: override",
              "children": [
              ]
            }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f9cd7916",
            "name": "Rebuild Table",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Rebuild Table\n\nSignature: void FormatTable()\nMethod: FormatTable\nReturns: void\n\nRebuild the selected rows (or the current line when no VISUAL\nselection is active) into a padded markdown table with a\n\"+---+\" separator, mirroring the web app's formatMarkdownTable.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "76f23bf7",
            "name": "Replace All Text",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Replace All Text\n\nSignature: void ReplaceAllInString(std::string& line, const std::string& old_text, const std::string& new_text, int& count)\nMethod: ReplaceAllInString\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    line     std::string&\n    old_text const std::string&\n    new_text const std::string&\n    count    int&\n\nReplace every occurrence of `old_text` in `line` with `new_text`,\ncounting the replacements.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f874bf8c",
            "name": "Replace Text",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Replace Text\n\nSignature: void ReplaceText(const std::string& args)\nMethod: ReplaceText\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    args const std::string&\n\nVim ':replace old/new' (also bound to 'R'): literal, global\nreplace of `old` with `new` inside the current node's text. In\nNORMAL mode the whole node text is processed (like :%s/../g);\nin VISUAL/VISUAL_LINE/VISUAL_BLOCK only the selected range is\ntouched. Only this node's text is ever changed.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "70d3e5b5",
            "name": "Replace Text in Range",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Replace Text in Range\n\nSignature: void ReplaceRange(std::string& line, int lo, int hi, const std::string& old_text, const std::string& new_text, int& count)\nMethod: ReplaceRange\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    line     std::string&\n    lo       int\n    hi       int\n    old_text const std::string&\n    new_text const std::string&\n    count    int&\n\nReplace within the half-open column range [lo, hi) of `line`.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "fd4ff245",
            "name": "Replaced Message",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Replaced Message\n\nSignature: void FinishReplace(int count)\nMethod: FinishReplace\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    count int",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "58c4ae22",
            "name": "Save Current File",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Save Current File\n\nSignature: void Save()\nMethod: Save\nReturns: void",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "28d34adf",
            "name": "Search Results Navigation",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Search Results Navigation\n\nSignature: void StepSearchOccurrence(int dir)\nMethod: StepSearchOccurrence\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    dir int\n\nStep the cursor to the next (dir > 0) or previous (dir < 0)\noccurrence of the active search query inside the current node's\ntext, wrapping around like Vim's n/N. Also works while the\nhighlight is hidden by ':noh' (the query is kept). Does nothing\nwhen there is no search or the node has no occurrences.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "4889b012",
            "name": "Search Word Under Cursor",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Search Word Under Cursor\n\nSignature: void SearchWordUnderCursor()\nMethod: SearchWordUnderCursor\nReturns: void\n\nVim '*': search for the word under the cursor and jump to its\nnext occurrence (wrapping). The word becomes the active find\nquery, so n/N continue stepping through it and the highlight\nshows every node that contains it.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "a9941d9f",
            "name": "Select First Search Match",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Select First Search Match\n\nSignature: void JumpToFirstSearchMatch()\nMethod: JumpToFirstSearchMatch\nReturns: void\n\nMove the cursor to the first occurrence of the active search\nquery in the freshly loaded node, so the '/' find and n/N\nnavigation reveal the match in the editor (as in Vim).",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "a222a350",
            "name": "Select Inner Word",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Select Inner Word\n\nSignature: void SelectInnerWord()\nMethod: SelectInnerWord\nReturns: void",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "fad06de1",
            "name": "Select Text",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Select Text\n\nSignature: std::string SelectionText() const\nMethod: SelectionText\nReturns: std::string\nQualifiers: const\n\nThe text currently under a VISUAL/VISUAL_LINE selection, or the\ncurrent line when no selection is active (NORMAL/INSERT).\nLine-based copies include a trailing newline so a cut+paste\nround-trip reproduces the lines.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "a78f1005",
            "name": "Selection to Lower",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Selection to Lower\n\nSignature: void LowerSelection()\nMethod: LowerSelection\nReturns: void\n\nVim 'u' (VISUAL): lowercase the selected text.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "fc6575a4",
            "name": "Selection to Upper",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Selection to Upper\n\nSignature: void UpperSelection()\nMethod: UpperSelection\nReturns: void\n\nVim 'U' (VISUAL): uppercase the selected text. Folding never\nchanges line count or line length, so nothing is erased or\nreassembled; the cursor is placed at the start of the selection\nand the mode returns to NORMAL.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "6ae5a092",
            "name": "Split Lines",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Split Lines\n\nSignature: static std::vector<std::string> SplitLines(const std::string& text)\nMethod: SplitLines\nReturns: static std::vector<std::string>\nParameters:\n    text const std::string&",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "fd8c4b6e",
            "name": "To Upper / To Lower",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "To Upper / To Lower\n\nSignature: static char ToUpperAscii(char c)\nMethod: ToUpperAscii\nReturns: static char\nParameters:\n    c char\n\nSignature: static char ToLowerAscii(char c)\nMethod: ToLowerAscii\nReturns: static char\nParameters:\n    c char\n\n                ASCII-only case folding: the editor is byte-oriented (columns =\n                bytes), so folding a full byte would corrupt UTF-8 text. Other\n                bytes (letters with diacritics, CJK, emoji, ...) are left as-is.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f0ae98ed",
            "name": "Transform Selection",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Transform Selection\n\nSignature: void TransformSelection(char (*fold)(char), const char* status_msg)\nMethod: TransformSelection\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    status_msg const char*",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "7807cbbb",
            "name": "Variables",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Variables\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::shared_ptr<EditorState> state_;\nscribbolyth::treeview::TreeNode* active_ = nullptr;\nstd::string active_id_;\nstd::vector<std::string> lines_;\nint row_ = 0;\nint col_ = 0;\nint last_col_ = 0;\nint visual_row_ = -1;\nint visual_col_ = -1;\nint viewport_height_ = 0;",
            "children": [
            ]
          }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "e0ffc710",
          "name": "Write to the Clipboard",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Write to the Clipboard\n\nSignature: bool WriteClipboard(const std::string& text)\nMethod: WriteClipboard\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    text const std::string&\n\nWrite to the system clipboard (Win32 API on Windows,\nwl-copy/xclip/xsel on POSIX). Returns false when no tool is\navailable.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "7fcc9d42",
          "name": "Make the Editor",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Make the Editor\n\nSignature: ftxui::Component MakeEditor(std::shared_ptr<EditorState> state)\nMethod: MakeEditor\nReturns: ftxui::Component\nParameters:\nstate std::shared_ptr<EditorState>",
          "children": [
          ]
        }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0af68024",
        "name": "editor_state.hpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "0277705b",
          "name": "Editor State Struct",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Editor State Struct",
          "children": [
          {
            "id": "4be4f201",
            "name": "Expand to Node",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Expand to Node\n\nSelect `node` in the tree, expanding every ancestor so it is visible.\nSet by the treeview.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::function<void(scribbolyth::treeview::TreeNode*)> reveal_node;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "6c0d499e",
            "name": "File Browser Related",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "File Browser Related\n\nFile browser dialog. `show_file_browser` is the Modal visibility flag;\n`browser_start_dir` is the directory to open in; `browser_pick` is\ninvoked with the chosen file's path when the user presses Enter.\n`browser_command` is the `:command` name of the invoking op for\nsave/export-style ops: when non-empty, Enter on a folder closes the\ndialog and reopens the command line prefilled with that folder so the\nuser can type a filename (open/import-style ops leave it empty and\nEnter on a folder simply navigates into it).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbool* show_file_browser = nullptr;\nstd::string browser_start_dir;\nstd::string browser_command;\nstd::function<void(const std::string&)> browser_pick;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "341b2976",
            "name": "Find in Node Related",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Find in Node Related\n\nVim-style find state (the last '/' search). `search_matches` holds the\nnodes that matched the last query, in document order; `search_index` is\nthe currently selected match (n/N move it, wrapping). `search_active`\nis cleared by ':noh' to hide the match highlight; the query and match\nlist are kept so n/N keep working, as in Vim.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::string search_query;\nstd::vector<scribbolyth::treeview::TreeNode*> search_matches;\nint search_index = -1;\nbool search_active = false;\n\n// Set when a '/' find executes; the editor consumes it to move its cursor\n// to the first occurrence in the (possibly unchanged) active node so the\n// match is revealed in the text, as in Vim.\nbool search_reveal_pending = false;\n\n// Step to the next (dir > 0) or previous (dir < 0) find result. Set by the\n// editor: it moves the cursor through the occurrences of the query inside\n// the active node's text (wrapping within the node), as in Vim.\nstd::function<void(int)> search_jump;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "b9534292",
            "name": "Focus",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Focus\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::function<void()> focus_editor;\nstd::function<void()> focus_treeview;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "6e90fb60",
            "name": "Getting All Nodes",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Getting All Nodes\n\nFlat enumeration of the document: (node pointer, depth) in document\norder, ignoring expansion state. Set by the treeview.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::function<std::vector<std::pair<scribbolyth::treeview::TreeNode*, int>>()> collect_all_nodes;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "694cfd28",
            "name": "Keep Command Open",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Keep Command Open\n\nWhen a command sets this on Enter (e.g. :calc leaving its result in the\nfield), the command line stays open with the buffer the command wrote\ninstead of closing. The Enter handler consumes and resets it.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbool command_keep_open = false;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "3fbceae2",
            "name": "Key Map Related",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Key Map Related\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKeymap normal_keymap;\nKeymap insert_keymap;\nKeymap visual_keymap;\nKeymap visual_block_keymap;\nKeymap tree_keymap;\n\nKeymap& ActiveKeymap() {\n    switch (mode) {\n        case Mode::TREE:            return tree_keymap;\n        case Mode::INSERT:          return insert_keymap;\n        case Mode::VISUAL:\n        case Mode::VISUAL_LINE:     return visual_keymap;\n        case Mode::VISUAL_BLOCK:    return visual_block_keymap;\n        case Mode::COMMAND:         return normal_keymap;\n        default:                    return normal_keymap;\n    }\n}",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "3cdf6e72",
            "name": "Mode-Related Variables",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Mode-Related Variables\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMode mode = Mode::TREE;\nstd::string command_buffer;\nint command_cursor = 0;\nint* active_child = nullptr;\nMode mode_before_command = Mode::TREE;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "044c3ae9",
            "name": "Node Undo History",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Node Undo History\n\nDocument undo history. A snapshot is pushed before every content\nmutation (tree edits and text edits); `undo_stack` is newest last,\n`redo_stack` newest first. `snapshot_undo`/`apply_undo`/`clear_undo`\nare installed by the treeview. The undo dialog reads the stacks\ndirectly and applies a rollback through `apply_undo`.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::vector<UndoState> undo_stack;\nstd::vector<UndoState> redo_stack;\nstatic constexpr std::size_t kUndoMax = 50;\n\nstd::function<void()> snapshot_undo;\n// `index` 0 = newest snapshot.\nstd::function<void(std::size_t index)> apply_undo;\nstd::function<void()> clear_undo;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "8afacbc9",
            "name": "Operations and Commands",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Operations and Commands\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::map<std::string, scribbolyth::op::Operation> operations;\nstd::map<std::string, std::string> commands;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f5966244",
            "name": "Recent Files",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Recent Files\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::vector<std::string> recent_files;\nstatic constexpr std::size_t kRecentMax = 20;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "73783b1f",
            "name": "Reset Cursor Position",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Reset Cursor Position\n\nPosition the editor cursor on a 0-based line of the currently active\nnode. Set by the editor.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::function<void(int)> reveal_line;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "13dc4c67",
            "name": "Text Insertion",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Text Insertion\n\nInsert `text` into the currently active node at the editor cursor, as a\nsingle undoable edit. Set by the editor; used by dialogs to inject text\n(e.g. a node link picked from a search) at the cursor.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::function<void(const std::string&)> insert_text_at_cursor;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "35ff38d9",
            "name": "Theme Material",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Theme Material\n\nTheme material captured from a .html import, carried through the session\nso a later HTML export reproduces it (colors, grid, custom CSS).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nscribbolyth::html::HtmlTheme html_theme;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "7559f9ff",
            "name": "Tracking Changes",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Tracking Changes\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nbool changed = false;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "24e14259",
            "name": "Treeview Related",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Treeview Related\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nint treeview_width = kDefaultTreeviewWidth;\n\nscribbolyth::treeview::TreeNode* active_node = nullptr;\nstd::string status;\nstd::string template_path;\nstd::string init_path;\nstd::vector<scribbolyth::bookmark::Bookmark> bookmarks;",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ce10f919",
            "name": "Viewed Node History",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Viewed Node History\n\nViewed-node history: node ids of every selected node that has text,\nmost recent last, deduplicated, capped at kHistoryMax. Populated by\nthe treeview; the history dialog resolves ids to live nodes.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nstd::vector<std::string> history;\nstatic constexpr std::size_t kHistoryMax = 30;",
            "children": [
            ]
          }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "7b981567",
          "name": "Undo State Struct",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Undo State Struct\n\nA single undoable point-in-time snapshot of the document. `json` is the\nfull serialized state (tree + bookmarks + history + width); `preview` is\na short human label for the undo dialog's list.\n\nstruct UndoState {\n    std::string json;\n    std::string preview;\n};",
          "children": [
          ]
        }
        ]
      }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d0848599",
      "name": "help",
      "expanded": false,
