        "children": [
        {
          "id": "78dff0bd",
          "name": "Append Bookmark.",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Append Bookmark.\n\nSignature: void AppendBookmarksJson(std::string& out, const std::vector<bookmark::Bookmark>& bookmarks, const std::vector<TreeNode>& roots)\nMethod: AppendBookmarksJson\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    out       std::string&\n    bookmarks const std::vector<bookmark::Bookmark>&\n    roots     const std::vector<TreeNode>&\n\nSerialize bookmarks into the HTML app's format:\n  { \"id\", \"caption\", \"path\", \"line\"? }  with `line` being 1-based.\nBookmarks whose target node no longer exists are skipped.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1a6c442a",
          "name": "Append History Json",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Append History Json\n\nSignature: void AppendHistoryJson(std::string& out, const std::vector<std::string>& history, const std::vector<TreeNode>& roots)\nMethod: AppendHistoryJson\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    out     std::string&\n    history const std::vector<std::string>&\n    roots   const std::vector<TreeNode>&\n\nSerialize the viewed-node history into the HTML app's format:\n  { \"id\", \"title\" }  one entry per id, most recent last.\nEntries whose target node no longer exists are skipped.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "97bcaaee",
          "name": "Append Node",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Append Node\n\nSignature: void AppendNode(std::string& out, const TreeNode& node, int depth)\nMethod: AppendNode\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    out   std::string&\n    node  const TreeNode&\n    depth int",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b64caf86",
          "name": "AsciiPunctuationInNode",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "AsciiPunctuationInNode\n\nSignature: void AsciiPunctuationInNode(TreeNode& node)\nMethod: AsciiPunctuationInNode\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    node TreeNode&\n\nConvert typographic punctuation in the imported titles and note text\nto plain ASCII, mirroring the paste sanitizer, so nothing that the\nterminal cannot render ends up in the document.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "41ddefed",
          "name": "Const Variables",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Const Variables\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nconst char* kThemeStyleOpen = \"<style id=\\\"theme_styles\\\">\";\nconst char* kThemeStyleClose = \"</style>\";",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "8e898875",
          "name": "Expand Tabs",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Expand Tabs\n\nSignature: void ExpandTabs(std::string& s)\nMethod: ExpandTabs\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    s std::string&\n\nThe web app renders leading indentation as literal tabs; the editor\nuses 4-space indentation (Tab inserts four spaces), so expanding each\ntab in the imported note text to four spaces keeps that leading\nwhitespace from being lost.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "38357821",
          "name": "ExpandTabsInNode",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "ExpandTabsInNode\n\nSignature: void ExpandTabsInNode(TreeNode& node)\nMethod: ExpandTabsInNode\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    node TreeNode&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b6de4007",
          "name": "Export Content",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Export Content\n\nSignature: std::string ExportContent(const TreeNode& node)\nMethod: ExportContent\nReturns: std::string\nParameters:\n    node const TreeNode&\n\nThe exported content keeps the note's text, but if its first line is\nnot already the node's name, the name is prepended on its own line so\nevery note reads as a titled section in the rendered HTML. Notes\nwith no text are left untouched (no title line is invented for them).",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "52fe2848",
          "name": "Export Html File",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Export Html File\n\nSignature: bool ExportHtmlFile(const std::string& template_path, const std::string& out_path, const std::vector<TreeNode>& roots, const std::vector<bookmark::Bookmark>& bookmarks, const std::vector<std::string>& history, const HtmlTheme* theme)\nMethod: ExportHtmlFile\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    template_path const std::string&\n    out_path      const std::string&\n    roots         const std::vector<TreeNode>&\n    bookmarks     const std::vector<bookmark::Bookmark>&\n    history       const std::vector<std::string>&\n    theme         const HtmlTheme*",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a2b3ab97",
          "name": "Find JS Array",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find JS Array\n\nSignature: bool FindJsArray(const std::string& html, const std::string& keyword, std::size_t& open, std::size_t& close)\nMethod: FindJsArray\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    html    const std::string&\n    keyword const std::string&\n    open    std::size_t&\n    close   std::size_t&\n\nLocate the '[' that opens the `let <keyword> = [ ... ];` array and the\nindex of its matching ']' (string- and nesting-aware). The keyword is\nmatched as a JS variable declaration so mentions of it in comments or\nhelp text never confuse the search.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4d99ab3b",
          "name": "Find JS Statement",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find JS Statement\n\nSignature: bool FindJsStatement(const std::string& html, const std::string& keyword, std::size_t& start, std::size_t& end)\nMethod: FindJsStatement\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    html    const std::string&\n    keyword const std::string&\n    start   std::size_t&\n    end     std::size_t&\n\nLocate a `let <keyword> = <value>;` script statement and return the\nbyte range [start, end) covering the whole statement including the\ntrailing ';'. The value may be a nested '{...}'/'[...]' literal,\nscanned string- and nesting-aware, or a scalar ending at ';'.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c9075132",
          "name": "Find Node by Id",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find Node by Id",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d82797e7",
          "name": "Find Style Content",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find Style Content\n\nSignature: bool FindStyleContent(const std::string& html, std::size_t& open, std::size_t& close)\nMethod: FindStyleContent\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    html  const std::string&\n    open  std::size_t&\n    close std::size_t&\n\nThe inner text of the `<style id=\"theme_styles\">` block.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
