        "name": "search.cpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "3b17656f",
          "name": "All Words Regex",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "All Words Regex\n\nSignature: std::string AllWordsRegex(const std::string& query)\nMethod: AllWordsRegex\nReturns: std::string\nParameters:\n    query const std::string&\n\nBuilds `(?=[\\s\\S]*\\bw1\\b)(?=[\\s\\S]*\\bw2\\b)...(?=[\\s\\S]*\\bwn\\b)[\\s\\S]*`\nfrom the whitespace-separated words of `query`, requiring every word\nto be present anywhere in the text (any order, any line). `[\\s\\S]`\nis the ECMAScript stand-in for DOTALL, so words on different lines\nstill satisfy the lookaheads.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6bf99daf",
          "name": "Collect Tags",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Collect Tags\n\nSignature: void CollectTags(const std::string& text, std::map<std::string, int>& counts)\nMethod: CollectTags\nReturns: void\nParameters:\n    text   const std::string&\n    counts std::map<std::string, int>&\n\nCollect `#tag` tokens from `text` into `counts` (keyed by lowercase\ntag, so the map iteration is sorted and de-duplicated). HTML color\ncodes such as \"#fff\" or \"#ff8800\" are ignored.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6e655bed",
          "name": "Contains Tag",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Contains Tag\n\nSignature: bool ContainsTag(const std::string& text, const std::string& tag)\nMethod: ContainsTag\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    text const std::string&\n    tag  const std::string&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6f6ee854",
          "name": "Create Search Results",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Create Search Results\n\nSignature: treeview::TreeNode* CreateSearchResults(std::shared_ptr<EditorState> state, const std::vector<treeview::TreeNode*>& nodes, const std::string& raw_query, std::string* status)\nMethod: CreateSearchResults\nReturns: treeview::TreeNode*\nParameters:\n    state     std::shared_ptr<EditorState>\n    nodes     const std::vector<treeview::TreeNode*>&\n    raw_query const std::string&\n    status    std::string*",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6fc5e374",
          "name": "Escape Regex",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Escape Regex\n\nSignature: std::string EscapeRegex(const std::string& s)\nMethod: EscapeRegex\nReturns: std::string\nParameters:\n    s const std::string&\n\nEscape the ECMAScript metacharacters so an \"all words\" search term\nkeeps its literal meaning inside the generated regex.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "df0cac25",
          "name": "Filter",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Filter\n\n!_method\n\nParsed search query: a leading \"r:\" selects case-insensitive regex\nmatching, a leading \":\" restricts the match to node titles and a\nleading \"+:\" requires every word to appear (in any order).",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "aed5c9ce",
          "name": "Find All Matches",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find All Matches\n\nSignature: std::vector<treeview::TreeNode*> FindAllMatches(std::shared_ptr<EditorState> state, const std::string& raw_query)\nMethod: FindAllMatches\nReturns: std::vector<treeview::TreeNode*>\nParameters:\n    state     std::shared_ptr<EditorState>\n    raw_query const std::string&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "2c5c8140",
          "name": "Find Line Matches",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find Line Matches\n\nSignature: std::vector<std::pair<int, int>> FindLineMatches(const std::string& line, const std::string& raw_query)\nMethod: FindLineMatches\nReturns: std::vector<std::pair<int, int>>\nParameters:\n    line      const std::string&\n    raw_query const std::string&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "2532e7a1",
          "name": "Find Matches",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find Matches\n\nSignature: std::vector<treeview::TreeNode*> FindMatches(std::shared_ptr<EditorState> state, const std::string& raw_query)\nMethod: FindMatches\nReturns: std::vector<treeview::TreeNode*>\nParameters:\n    state     std::shared_ptr<EditorState>\n    raw_query const std::string&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "0189a9bf",
          "name": "Indent Name",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Indent Name\n\nSignature: std::string IndentName(int depth, const std::string& name)\nMethod: IndentName\nReturns: std::string\nParameters:\n    depth int\n    name  const std::string&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c5a444d6",
          "name": "Is Hex Color",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Is Hex Color\n\nSignature: bool IsHexColor(const std::string& tag)\nMethod: IsHexColor\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    tag const std::string&\n\nA tag that is purely hex digits of length 3, 4, 6 or 8 (e.g. \"#fff\"\nor \"#ff8800\") is an HTML color, not a tag.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "e0496dfc",
          "name": "Is Regex Filter",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Is Regex Filter\n\nSignature: bool IsRegexFilter(const std::string& raw)\nMethod: IsRegexFilter\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    raw const std::string&\n\nWhether the filter runs a regex-based match (\"r:\" regex or\n\"+:\" all-words). These are deferred until Return is pressed so\nthat typing stays responsive instead of re-scanning the tree\n(and re-compiling a regex) on every keystroke.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "5a762413",
          "name": "Node Matches",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Node Matches\n\nSignature: bool NodeMatches(const treeview::TreeNode& node, const Filter& f, bool* regex_error)\nMethod: NodeMatches\nReturns: bool\nParameters:\n    node        const treeview::TreeNode&\n    f           const Filter&\n    regex_error bool*\n\nCase-insensitive match of a node against a parsed filter. An empty\nquery matches everything. When `query` is a regex that fails to\ncompile, returns false and sets `*regex_error`.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fb4551b5",
          "name": "Pad Right",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Pad Right\n\nSignature: std::string PadRight(const std::string& s, std::size_t width)\nMethod: PadRight\nReturns: std::string\nParameters:\n    s     const std::string&\n    width std::size_t",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b749e04c",
          "name": "Parse Filter",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Parse Filter\n\nSignature: Filter ParseFilter(const std::string& raw)\nMethod: ParseFilter\nReturns: Filter\nParameters:\n    raw const std::string&",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "bc74a7c2",
          "name": "Result Struct",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Result Struct\n\nstruct Result\n{\n    treeview::TreeNode* node;\n    std::string line;\n};",
          "children": [
