      {
        "id": "232eb493",
        "name": "search.hpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "cb2d7c57",
          "name": "Dialog Mode Enum",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Dialog Mode Enum\n\nHow the search dialog's Enter key behaves.\n\nenum class DialogMode\n{\n    Jump,          // Enter jumps to the selected node.\n    InsertLink,    // Enter inserts a _Title_ link at the editor cursor.\n    CreateResults, // Enter creates a new \"Search results: <query>\" node\n                   // holding one _Title_ link per matching node.\n};",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ddb357c5",
          "name": "Find Matches",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Find Matches\n\nstd::vector<scribbolyth::treeview::TreeNode*> FindMatches(\n    std::shared_ptr<EditorState> state, const std::string& raw_query);\n\nstd::vector<std::pair<int, int>> FindLineMatches(const std::string& line,\n                                                 const std::string& raw_query);\n\nFind matches for `raw_query` inside the currently active node only\n(the same prefix rules as the search dialog apply: a leading \"r:\" makes\nit a case-insensitive regex, a leading \":\" restricts it to node titles,\notherwise it is a case-insensitive substring match). Returns either the\nactive node (when it matches) or nothing, so the Vim-style '/' find and\nn/N navigation stay confined to the node being edited.",
          "children": [
          {
            "id": "2544a033",
            "name": "Create Search Results",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Create Search Results\n\n!_method\n\nCreate a new node named \"Search results: <query>\" whose body holds one\n`_Title_` link per matching node (entries with no node pointer are\nskipped). The node is created like a normal new child: as the first\nchild of the tree selection when one is selected, otherwise as a root\nnode, and becomes the active node. Returns the created node, or nullptr\non failure (e.g. no matches to link). `status` receives a short\nuser-facing message.",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "d7aca825",
            "name": "Find All Matches",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Find All Matches\n\n!_method\n\nDocument-wide search: every node whose title or content satisfies\n`raw_query`, in document order, using the same prefix rules as\nFindMatches (\"r:\" regex, \"+:\" all words, \":\" titles only).",
            "children": [
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "9ea7005e",
            "name": "Make Search Dialog",
            "expanded": false,
            "text": "Make Search Dialog\n\n!_method\n\nBuild the node search/filter dialog. While *show is true it consumes\nevery event, so no app key bindings fire. ArrowUp/ArrowDown move the\nselection, Enter behaves per `mode` and closes (creating a results node\nalso collects it), Escape cancels. A leading \"r:\" makes the query a\ncase-insensitive regex, \"+:\" requires every word and \":\" restricts the\nmatch to node titles. The dialog keeps a fixed size regardless of\nresult count.",
            "children": [
            ]
          }
          ]
        }
        ]
      }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e6d5c8c8",
      "name": "text",
      "expanded": false,
      "text": "",
      "children": [
      {
        "id": "d81de6bf",
        "name": "text.cpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "b9c1d8c8",
          "name": "Punctuation Vector",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Punctuation Vector\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nconst std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>>& PunctuationMap()\n{\n    static const std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>> kMap = {\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x98\", \"'\"},    // U+2018 left single quote\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x99\", \"'\"},    // U+2019 right single quote\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x9A\", \"'\"},    // U+201A low single quote\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x9C\", \"\\\"\"},   // U+201C left double quote\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x9D\", \"\\\"\"},   // U+201D right double quote\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x9E\", \"\\\"\"},   // U+201E low double quote\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x93\", \"-\"},    // U+2013 en dash\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\x94\", \"-\"},    // U+2014 em dash\n        {\"\\xE2\\x80\\xA6\", \"...\"},  // U+2026 ellipsis\n        {\"\\xE2\\x88\\x92\", \"-\"},    // U+2212 minus sign\n    };\n    return kMap;\n}",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "584b1213",
          "name": "To Ascii Punctuation",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "To Ascii Punctuation\n\nSignature: std::string ToAsciiPunctuation(const std::string& text)\nMethod: ToAsciiPunctuation\nReturns: std::string\nParameters:\n    text const std::string&\n\nReplaces special characters with their ASCII equivalents.",
          "children": [
          ]
        }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "86f8f810",
        "name": "text.hpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "2a99ba0c",
          "name": "Ascii to Punctuation",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Ascii to Punctuation\n\n!_method\n\nReplace typographic (smart) punctuation with plain ASCII equivalents so\nthe result is always renderable in the terminal (\"smart\" quote/dash\ncharacters often do not display). Only the exact UTF-8 sequences of the\nmapped characters are consumed; every other byte, including other\nmulti-byte characters, passes through untouched.",
          "children": [
          ]
        }
        ]
      }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3578f956",
      "name": "treeview",
      "expanded": false,
      "text": "",
      "children": [
      {
        "id": "ccd3a286",
        "name": "tree_node.hpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "0ab1dee5",
          "name": "Tree Node Struct",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Tree Node Struct\n\nstruct TreeNode\n{\n    std::string id;\n    std::string name;\n    bool expanded = false;\n    std::string text;\n    std::vector<TreeNode> children;\n};",
          "children": [
          ]
        }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "71858e59",
        "name": "treeview.cpp",
        "expanded": false,
        "text": "",
        "children": [
        {
          "id": "ca37fe8e",
          "name": "Introduction",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Introduction\n\nTreeView is the notes sidebar tree: an FTXUI component that owns the\ndocument's node tree, the current selection, and all tree-mode behavior:\n\n  - selection / cursor movement across the visible tree (j/k, gg/G, /find)\n  - structural edits: add, rename, delete and move nodes, expand & collapse\n  - document persistence: open, save, import and export\n  - undo history, scoped to the currently selected node\n  - the record of viewed nodes that powers the history dialog\n\nTreeView installs callbacks into EditorState.operations under formal op\nnames (\"move_up\", \"new_node\", ...). The tree keymap in commands.conf maps\nkeys to those names and op::HandleKey()/op::Dispatch() invoke the matching\ncallback, so this file contains no key-decoding logic of its own.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "38866250",
          "name": "Apply Undo",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Apply Undo\n\nSignature: void TreeView::ApplyUndo(std::size_t index)\nMethod: ApplyUndo\nReturns: void TreeView\nParameters:\n    index std::size_t\n\nRoll back to undo entry `index` (0 = newest): move the current state to\nthe redo stack, drop newer undos, reload the stored tree, and re-find\nthe previously selected node by id.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4e4cf818",
          "name": "Browse For File",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Browse For File\n\nSignature: void TreeView::BrowseFor(const std::string& dir, const std::string& command, std::function<void(const std::string&)> on_pick)\nMethod: BrowseFor\nReturns: void TreeView\nParameters:\n    dir     const std::string&\n    command const std::string&\n    on_pick std::function<void(const std::string&)>\n\nOpen the file-browser dialog. `on_pick` runs when a file is chosen; when\n`command` is non-empty, choosing a folder instead reopens the command\nline prefilled with it (the save/export flow).",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fd04b2dd",
          "name": "Clear Undo",
          "expanded": false,
          "text": "Clear Undo\n\nSignature: void TreeView::ClearUndo()\nMethod: ClearUndo\nReturns: void TreeView\n\nDrop both the undo and redo stacks.",
          "children": [
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a75de894",
          "name": "Collapse All",
          "expanded": false,
